## Constraints inherited

See `ops/rules.constraints.hybrid` (anchored). Slice-3 specific reinforcement:
- Inline prompt version line is now ENFORCED. First line of every runtime prompt template:
  `# prompt: <name> v<version>`
  Anything calling a prompt without parsing & logging this version: reject in code review.
- No autonomous sending — the approve endpoint records intent, never transmits.
- Provider abstraction: do not import `openai` (or any provider SDK) outside the adapter module.

---

## Resolved decisions (coordinator)

```
provider           OpenAI-compatible Python client (works with Mistral, OpenAI, Ollama, etc.)
                   point LLM_API_BASE_URL at the provider; default in .env.example: Mistral
                   builder uses the official `openai` Python SDK with custom base_url
                   (matches user's existing Mistral experience while keeping options open)

LiteLLM            skip · revisit when 2+ providers active

OCR                skip · slice-5

PDF parsing        skip · slice-4 will add pdfplumber for text-PDFs

worker queue       FastAPI BackgroundTasks · move to Celery+Redis when retry/long jobs needed

schema scope       MVP-minimum: documents · document_analyses · audit_events · prompt_runs
                   defer: users · workspaces · document_chunks · suggested_actions · evaluations

auth               none · single-tenant · localhost-only for now

repo restructure   first task of slice-3 (so subsequent code lands in the right place)

analyzer modularity  pluggable Analyzer protocol from day one · registry-based dispatch
                     slice-3 ships only InvoiceExtractor · slice-4 adds Classifier + Summarizer +
                     ContractReviewer as new files in app/analyzers/ — no pipeline refactor needed
                     each Analyzer has: name · version · applies_to: set[DocType] · run(doc)
                     multiple analyzers may run on one doc · they write different fields
                     into DocumentAnalysis (classifier→type+confidence · summarizer→summary ·
                     extractor→fields/missing/risk · reviewer→risk_flags+terms)
                     each analyzer call creates its own PromptRun row (full audit trail)

input format       text only (.txt or pasted) · upload UI takes a textarea + filename
                   builder must NOT introduce PDF parsing in this slice

doc type           user-selected on upload (dropdown) · no auto-classification yet
                   slice-3 only validates type === supplier_invoice for the extractor pipeline
                   uploads of other types: save document, no analysis run, audit "not_supported_yet"

inbox display      slice-3 hides slice-2's 12 non-invoice mocks from /app/inbox
                   /demo keeps them as static marketing content
                   /app/ask qa.ts unchanged (still references the 16-doc mock set)
```

---

## API contract (initial)

```
POST /api/documents
  multipart/form-data
    text:     string  (required · the document body)
    filename: string  (required · e.g., "invoice_lumina.txt")
    type:     enum    (required · supplier_invoice | client_invoice | contract |
                       supplier_offer | client_request | accountant_request |
                       hr_document | internal_procedure | price_list | unknown)
  → 202 { id, status: "queued" }

GET /api/documents
  → 200 [{ id, filename, type, status, created_at, urgency? }]

GET /api/documents/:id
  → 200 { document, analysis, audit_events }
        analysis: null until pipeline finishes
        analysis.fields[] · analysis.missing_fields[] · analysis.risk_flags[]
        analysis.summary (null in slice-3 — summary prompt is slice-4)
        analysis.suggested_action (null in slice-3)

POST /api/documents/:id/approve
  → 200 { document_id, approved_at } · appends audit event

GET /api/audit?limit=50
  → 200 [{ id, document_id?, event_type, event_data, created_at }]

GET /api/health → 200 { status: "ok" }
```

---

## Prompt template (invoice_extractor v1)

Builder writes `apps/api/app/prompts/invoice_extractor_v1.txt` with:
- First line: `# prompt: invoice_extractor v1`
- Adapt prompt 19.16 from `codocz/romanian_sme_ai_companion_prompt_pack.md` verbatim for the body
- Inject DOCUMENT_TEXT via simple `{{DOCUMENT_TEXT}}` substitution (no Jinja yet)
- Output validated against Pydantic schema mirroring the JSON skeleton in §19.16

When the prompt is loaded, the runner:
1. Parses the first line for `# prompt: <name> v<version>`
2. Records both in the prompt_runs row
3. Stores the substituted full prompt as input_text + a sha256 in input_hash

