2. INFRA — POSTGRES VIA DOCKER COMPOSE.
   - infra/docker-compose.yml: single service `postgres:16` on port 5432, named volume, env vars from .env.
   - infra/.env.example: POSTGRES_USER · POSTGRES_PASSWORD · POSTGRES_DB · LLM_API_BASE_URL · LLM_API_KEY · LLM_MODEL.
   - Document in apps/api/README.md how to run: cd infra && docker compose up -d postgres.
   - Commit: "slice-3(infra): postgres docker-compose + env example"

3. FASTAPI SCAFFOLD.
   - apps/api/pyproject.toml using uv (or poetry — your call; record in patchlog).
   - apps/api/app/ structure: main.py · api/ · core/ · db/ · models/ · schemas/ · services/ · prompts/ · workers/.
   - Dependencies: fastapi · uvicorn · sqlalchemy · alembic · pydantic · pydantic-settings · python-multipart · openai (used as OpenAI-compatible client) · psycopg2-binary or psycopg[binary].
   - core/config.py: Pydantic BaseSettings reading from .env.
   - db/session.py: SQLAlchemy engine + sessionmaker.
   - main.py: FastAPI app with CORS for localhost:5173 · health endpoint · API router prefix /api.
   - Verify: uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload starts cleanly · curl localhost:8000/api/health returns {"status":"ok"}.
   - Commit: "slice-3(api): FastAPI scaffold · config · session · health"

4. ALEMBIC + MODELS.
   - Initialize alembic: cd apps/api && uv run alembic init -t async alembic (or sync — your call).
   - Configure alembic env.py to read from app.core.config and app.db.models.
   - Models in app/db/models/ (one file per model OR a single models.py — your call):
       Document(id UUID, filename str, type str, status str, raw_text Text, created_at, updated_at)
       DocumentAnalysis(id UUID, document_id FK, prompt_run_id FK,
                        fields JSONB, missing_fields JSONB, risk_flags JSONB,
                        summary Text nullable, suggested_action Text nullable,
                        created_at)
       AuditEvent(id UUID, document_id FK nullable, event_type str, event_data JSONB, created_at)
       PromptRun(id UUID, document_id FK nullable, prompt_name str, prompt_version str,
                 model str, input_text Text, input_hash str, output_json JSONB nullable,
                 status str, error_message Text nullable, created_at, completed_at nullable)
   - Generate the initial migration: alembic revision --autogenerate -m "initial schema"
   - Run: alembic upgrade head — verify 4 tables exist in postgres.
   - Commit: "slice-3(api): alembic + 4 initial models · documents · analyses · audit · prompt_runs"

5. PROVIDER ADAPTER + PROMPT LOADER.
   - app/services/llm.py: a thin adapter wrapping the OpenAI Python SDK with custom base_url. Single function: complete(prompt: str, model: str | None = None) -> str. Reads LLM_* env vars. Do NOT import openai outside this module.
   - app/services/prompts.py: load_prompt(name) reads apps/api/app/prompts/<name>_<version>.txt, parses the first line for `# prompt: <name> v<version>`, returns (template, name, version). Provide substitute(template, vars) for `{{VAR}}` placeholder replacement.
   - Commit: "slice-3(api): provider adapter + prompt loader"

6. ANALYZER FRAMEWORK + INVOICE EXTRACTOR.
   - app/analyzers/base.py: Analyzer Protocol with `name: str`, `version: str`, `applies_to: set[DocType]`, async `run(document) -> AnalyzerResult`. AnalyzerResult is a small Pydantic class carrying: analyzer_name · analyzer_version · prompt_input · prompt_output_raw · parsed_output (Any) · status ("success"|"failed") · error_message (optional).
   - app/analyzers/registry.py: ANALYZERS list and `analyzers_for(doc) -> list[Analyzer]` returning every analyzer where doc.type in applies_to.
   - app/analyzers/merge.py: `merge_into_analysis(doc_analysis, result)` function that knows how each analyzer's parsed_output maps to columns of DocumentAnalysis (slice-3 only handles InvoiceExtraction → fields/missing_fields/risk_flags; slice-4 will extend it for classifier/summary/contract — keep this function easy to extend with isinstance dispatch or a per-analyzer mapper).
   - app/schemas/extraction.py: Pydantic InvoiceExtraction schema mirroring codocz/romanian_sme_ai_companion_prompt_pack.md §19.16 JSON.
   - app/prompts/invoice_extractor_v1.txt: first line `# prompt: invoice_extractor v1`, body adapted from §19.16 with {{DOCUMENT_TEXT}} placeholder.
   - app/analyzers/invoice_extractor.py: class InvoiceExtractor implementing the protocol. applies_to = {"supplier_invoice"}. run() loads prompt, substitutes text, calls llm.complete, parses JSON, validates against InvoiceExtraction schema, returns AnalyzerResult.
   - Register InvoiceExtractor in registry.ANALYZERS.
   - Commit: "slice-3(api): analyzer framework + InvoiceExtractor v1 (first registered analyzer)"

7. PIPELINE + ENDPOINTS.
   - app/services/analysis.py: `run_analysis(document_id)` — loads doc, calls analyzers_for(doc); for each analyzer: invoke run(), merge_into_analysis the result, persist a PromptRun row (success/failure with error_message), append AuditEvent ("analyzed_by:<analyzer.name>"). If no analyzers applicable: append AuditEvent "not_supported_yet" and leave analysis null.
   - app/api/documents.py: POST /api/documents (multipart) → save Document, schedule BackgroundTask(run_analysis). GET /api/documents (list, ordered by created_at desc). GET /api/documents/:id (detail with analysis + audit). POST /api/documents/:id/approve (audit event).
   - app/api/audit.py: GET /api/audit?limit=50.
   - Wire routers into main.py.
   - Commit: "slice-3(api): pipeline (registry dispatch) + documents + audit endpoints"

8. SEED SCRIPT.
   - apps/api/scripts/seed_invoices.py: reads the 4 invoice docs from apps/web/src/lib/data/inbox.ts (or hand-copies their rawContent — your call). Posts each to /api/documents as type=supplier_invoice. Prints document IDs and waits for analysis to complete (poll GET /api/documents/:id every 2s for up to 60s).
   - Run it manually, verify all 4 succeed, capture one extraction in your patchlog summary.
   - Commit: "slice-3(api): seed script for 4 invoices + verified end-to-end"

9. FRONTEND WIRING.
   - apps/web/src/lib/api/client.ts: typed fetch wrappers for the 5 endpoints. Read VITE_API_BASE_URL from env, default http://localhost:8000.
   - apps/web/src/routes/app/inbox/+page.svelte: replace static INBOX_DOCS import with API fetch. Loading state · empty state · error state. Map API response to the existing UI shape (extraction.fields → ExtractedField[] etc).
   - Add an Upload UI: textarea + filename input + type dropdown + Submit button. On submit: POST /api/documents, optimistic add to list with status="queued", then poll the doc until analysis arrives.
   - Show "Live" badge on cards backed by API data.
   - Hide slice-2's 12 non-invoice mocks from /app/inbox (do NOT delete inbox.ts — /demo and /app/ask still reference parts of it; you may need to split: e.g., move the 12 to a separate export `MOCK_DEMO_DOCS` used only by /demo).
   - Verify: with backend up + seed run, /app/inbox shows the 4 invoices as "Live" with correct extractions.
   - Commit: "slice-3(web): API client + /app/inbox wired to backend + upload UI"

10. ACCEPTANCE.
    - Run through every line of slice-3 §Acceptance manually. Note any deviations.
