## Hotfix · slice-3.1 (live verification revealed schema/LLM mismatch)

```
finding     analyzer pattern works · framework is sound
            but every invoice fails Pydantic validation:
              numeric fields declared `str`, LLM returns int/float
            secondary: document.status doesn't reflect analyzer outcome

scope IN    schema coercers + prompt nudge + status propagation + reseed + verify

scope OUT   prompt version bump  (this is a non-breaking refinement of v1 contract)
            new analyzers · new endpoints · UI changes · feature work
```

### Hotfix builder prompt

Copy into a fresh Sonnet session at the repo root:

```text
Read CLAUDE.md and ops/slice-3.backend.hybrid §Hotfix.

You are the builder for the slice-3 hotfix. Coordinator (opus) verified the live pipeline; all 5 invoices failed extraction due to a schema/LLM contract mismatch caught by the analyzer framework but not yet handled.

Root cause:
- apps/api/app/schemas/extraction.py declares total_amount, vat_amount, and line_items inner numeric fields as `str | None`. LLM returns these as JSON numbers (3046.4, 12, 185). Pydantic raises 8 validation errors per document.

Secondary bug:
- apps/api/app/services/analysis.py sets Document.status = "done" even when the analyzer fails. Status should reflect actual analyzer outcome.

Tasks (commit at each numbered checkpoint):

1. SCHEMA COERCERS.
   In apps/api/app/schemas/extraction.py:
   - Keep numeric field types as `str | None` (UI expects strings).
   - Add a Pydantic field_validator with mode="before" that coerces incoming int/float to str:
       monetary fields (total_amount, vat_amount, line_items[].unit_price, line_items[].amount)
         → format as "{value:.2f}"
       integer fields (line_items[].quantity)
         → str(int(value))
   - If the value is None or already a str, pass through.
   - Use a single shared validator helper if cleaner.
   Commit: "slice-3-hotfix(schema): coerce numeric fields to strings before validation"

2. PROMPT NUDGE.
   In apps/api/app/prompts/invoice_extractor_v1.txt:
   - Add to the rules section a brief line: "Return amounts as decimal strings (e.g., \"3046.40\"); return quantities as integer strings (e.g., \"12\"); use null for missing values."
   - Do NOT bump the version. This is a non-breaking refinement of v1; coercers in step 1 already handle either format. (If you strongly disagree, bump to v1.1 and update the inline `# prompt:` line; record why in patchlog.)
   Commit: "slice-3-hotfix(prompt): clarify number formatting in invoice_extractor v1"

3. STATUS PROPAGATION.
   In apps/api/app/services/analysis.py (run_analysis or equivalent):
   - After running all applicable analyzers for a document:
       if at least one analyzer succeeded   → Document.status = "done"
       if every analyzer failed              → Document.status = "failed"
       if no analyzers applied               → Document.status = "not_supported"
   - Also update GET /api/documents list response to expose status accurately.
   Commit: "slice-3-hotfix(api): document.status reflects analyzer outcome"

4. WIPE + RESEED.
   - Wipe doc-related tables. Pick whichever is least friction:
       a) docker compose exec postgres psql -U <user> -d <db> -c "TRUNCATE documents, document_analyses, audit_events, prompt_runs CASCADE;"
       b) cd apps/api && uv run alembic downgrade base && uv run alembic upgrade head
   - Re-run: uv run python scripts/seed_invoices.py
   - All 5 should land with status="done" and populated analysis.

5. VERIFY (the slice-3 acceptance lines that were red).
   - curl http://localhost:8000/api/documents | jq '.[] | {filename, status}'
       all 5 should be "done"
   - curl http://localhost:8000/api/documents/<lumina_id> | jq .analysis
       expected fields:
         supplier_name = "Lumina Design SRL"
         supplier_cui  = "RO00000001"
         invoice_number= "LD 0041"  (or close)
         invoice_date  = "28.04.2026"
         due_date      = "12.05.2026"
         total_amount  = "3046.40"
         currency      = "RON"
         missing_fields includes the PO reference (or equivalent)
   - prompt_runs: SELECT prompt_name, prompt_version, status FROM prompt_runs;
       5 rows, all status="success"
   - Open http://localhost:5173/app/inbox in browser → 5 Live cards with extracted fields visible.

6. SHIP.
   - Append ONE PATCHLOG line to ops/slice-3.backend.hybrid (hotfix verified · model used · timing).
   - Append ONE PATCHLOG line to ops/project.state.hybrid; update §Now (current → slice-4) only after all 5 verify clean.
   - Final commit: "slice-3-hotfix: live extraction verified · 5/5 invoices · slice-3 truly stable"

Hard rules (unchanged from slice-3):
- never call provider SDK outside app/services/llm.py
- inline prompt version line on every runtime prompt
- no Send button anywhere · ever

If verification step 5 shows ANY hallucinated value (e.g., a CUI or amount not in the source text), STOP and report. Do not proceed to ship until extraction is clean.
```

